@startuml
title From one random draw to a confidence interval (MIT 6.0002, lecture 7)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}

rectangle "Population\nany distribution with mean mu\nand finite variance sigma^2\n(uniform die, roulette, needle hit/miss)" as P
rectangle "Sample of size n\nX1 ... Xn, independent,\nsame distribution" as S
rectangle "Sample mean\nXbar = (X1 + ... + Xn) / n" as M
rectangle "Central limit theorem\nXbar approx. Normal(mu, sigma^2 / n)\nfor large n" as C
rectangle "Empirical rule\n68.27 % within 1 SE\n95.00 % within 1.96 SE\n99.73 % within 3 SE" as E
rectangle "95 % confidence interval\nXbar +/- 1.96 s / sqrt(n)" as CI
rectangle "Simulation model\n(code that generates the X_i)" as SIM

SIM --> P : defines
P --> S : draw
S --> M : average
M --> C : distribution of
C --> E : licenses
E --> CI : gives
note right of CI
  Covers E[Xbar] in about 95 % of repetitions.
  E[Xbar] equals the real quantity
  only if the model is right.
end note
@enduml
